            <ArticleTitle>[The clinical picture of acute tuberculosis (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>587-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical picture of acute tuberculosis infection is undergoing a change. The classic symptoms of pain in the chest and night sweats are giving way to general symptoms. In 50% of the cases the infection manifests itself as an acute disease. The observation that some cases of tuberculosis are not admitted to hospital until they are in a critical condition is ascribed to lack of &quot;tuberculosis awareness&quot;.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
